# Level-5 Reference Contract

## Authoritative semantic source

Identify the canonical ontology/configuration source. Generated artifacts and hand-maintained catalogs are projections, not competing authorities.

## Ontology, classes, and properties

Document the admitted domain vocabulary and identifiers projected by the pack.

## Generated surfaces

Enumerate every generated output class and the source/query/template path that manufactures it.

## Gates and refusals

Enumerate admission gates, typed refusal codes, and the conditions that trigger them. Missing or contradictory facts must fail closed.

## Configuration

Document admitted configuration, defaults, bounds, and the source of each operational value.

## Commands

List the canonical generation, validation, qualification, receipt-verification, and replay commands.

## Receipts and replay

Specify receipt identity fields, consequence binding, verification behavior, replay inputs, and replay mismatch semantics.

## Authority

Specify SELECT, CONSTRUCT, and DO boundaries. No generated surface or semantic derivation gains ambient execution authority.

## Dependencies and composition

Document required pack/runtime dependencies, composition order, compatibility constraints, and dependency-closure expectations.

## Compatibility

Record supported versions and typed UNSUPPORTED/REFUSED boundaries. Compatibility metadata must not silently widen authority.

## Maturity standing

Reference facts describe obligations and observed evidence. ALIVE requires execution against the exact admitted subject.

## Canonical-source rule

Do not hand-maintain a second copy of canonical semantic facts. Prefer ontology -> query -> generation -> verification correspondence so drift is mechanically visible.
